  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How do I track a Ford Mustang Mach-E with no connected services?",
      "a": "Use a DIMO device, which is the connection type listed for this vehicle. Once it is connected and shared with your Developer License, you can query trips with the segments resource in the Telemetry API, which accepts a date range of up to 31 days."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect idling on a Ford Mustang Mach-E?",
      "a": "The AutoPi entry for this vehicle lists the idling event. Query segments in the Telemetry API with the idling mechanism, which requires a DIMO device and treats windows where engine RPM stays at or below maxIdleRpm as idle (default 1000)."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect recharge on a Ford Mustang Mach-E?",
      "a": "Both DIMO device entries list the recharge event. Query segments with the recharge mechanism, which uses charging signals and state of charge, and tune minIncreasePercent (default 15) to control how large a rise counts as a recharge."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I detect harsh braking on a Ford Mustang Mach-E?",
      "a": "The DIMO LTE R1 entry lists the harsh braking event. You can count it per trip by passing an eventRequests entry named HarshBraking to the segments query, or push it to your server in real time with a webhook on the events service using behavior.harshBraking."
    },
    {
      "q": "How do I verify Ford Mustang Mach-E mileage?",
      "a": "Both DIMO device entries list the odometer signal. Call the Attestation API's odometer-statement endpoint (POST /v2/attestation/odometer-statement/:tokenId) with a Vehicle JWT to generate a verifiable odometer attestation, then retrieve it through the Telemetry API."
    }
  ],
  "intro": "DIMO provides a Ford Mustang Mach-E vehicle data API through a DIMO device, for model years 2021 and newer, and this coverage has been tested. The DIMO LTE R1 and AutoPi both connect the EV this way, and you read its data from the Telemetry API, a GraphQL endpoint, using a Vehicle JWT. Vehicle owners consent to and control sharing, so builders get data with clear provenance."
